  "features": {
    "legacy_data_upgrade": {
      "what": "rewrites pre-26.3 data on load: block states, spawn override counts, loot function ids, conditions, typeless number ranges (core/msl_upgrade.py)",
      "mc_from": "26.3",
      "msl_from": "3.3.0",
      "source": "compat/LegacyDataUpgrader.java and mixins/resources/RegistryLoadTaskMixin.java, both '//? if >=26.3'; first in tag 3.3.0-26.3 (commit 2b31c44), unchanged through 3.4.2"
    },
    "trial_spawner_configs": {
      "what": "reads data/<ns>/trial_spawner/*.json where vanilla does not (before 1.21.2) and writes the config inline when its processor places the spawner",
      "mc_from": "1.21",
      "mc_until": "1.21.2",
      "msl_from": "3.0.0",
      "source": "misc/trialspawnerconfig/TrialSpawnerConfigManager.java ('//? if >=1.21.1 <26.1.2') and world/processors/TrialSpawnerRandomizingProcessor.java; first in tag 1.21.1-3.0.0 (commit 02c2aed). The JSON is copied to NBT as it is: mob data is not upgraded"
    }
  },
  "builds_source": "Every MSL file on Modrinth (project 1oUDhxuy, read 2026-11-08), per loader, with the version its loader compares (fabric.mod.json `version`, or mods.toml `version`). \"from\": \"jar\" is read from the jar itself (171 of the 334 files, matched by sha1); \"modrinth\" follows what every jar read shows: 1.x and 2.x Fabric jars carry a pre-release suffix (1.1.0-1.20-1.20.4, 2.0.2-fabric), which Fabric Loader orders below the release, while 3.x Fabric jars are releases (3.3.0 or 3.3.0+fabric); Forge and NeoForge jars carry the Modrinth version number. A Quilt player runs the Fabric build.",
